xt-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:116%"&gt;840&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:116%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:116%"&gt;854&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:124%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-bottom:2pt solid #000000;padding:2px 4.45pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:124%"&gt;4,245&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:20.16pt"&gt;Energy credit purchase obligation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:8.8pt;padding-left:43.5pt;padding-right:10.2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;The Company is required to meet a renewable portfolio standard compliance program in New Hampshire. This statute requires electricity provider to source a minimum portion of its resources from certain renewable or alternative energy resources. The Company incurs a compliance obligation throughout the year as electricity is sold to customers. To satisfy its compliance requirements, the Company periodically enters into stand-alone contracts to purchase renewable energy credits from third parties, and makes purchases throughout the year. As of December 31, 2025, the Company has an outstanding energy credit purchase obligation of $2,719 (2024 - $2,971).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:22.11pt"&gt;Shareholder&#8217;s capital&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is authorized to issue 60,400 common shares. As at December 31, 2025, 60,400 common shares are issued and outstanding, all held by Liberty Energy Utilities (New Hampshire) Corp. Par value is $100.00 per share.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:20.16pt"&gt;Income taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:4.85pt;padding-left:43.5pt;padding-right:10.35pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;The income tax expense in the statement of comprehensive income represents an effective tax rate different than U.S. enacted federal statutory income tax rate of 21.0% (2024 - 21.0%):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:0.55pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:43.85pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:91.220%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:38.214%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.028%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:13.418%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:13.418%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:13.422%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:center"/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:124%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:124%"&gt;Percentage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:1.7pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tahoma',san